<p>Port de Sóller itself sits in a natural horseshoe-shaped bay, a formation that has made it a working harbour and a sheltered anchorage for generations before it became a visitor destination. The town retains a genuine, lived-in character distinct from purpose-built resort areas elsewhere on the island, with a working fishing fleet, a seafront promenade lined with cafés, and the vintage tram line linking the port to Sóller town a short distance inland.</p>
